Runtime: State

Purpose:
  Defines runtime state for crash recovery, session management,
  and orchestrator coordination. This is the single source of truth
  for runtime current state.

State:
  Mode: AUTO | SUPERVISED | STRICT | AUDIT | READ_ONLY
  Project: <project-name>
  SessionID: SESSION-<timestamp>-<random>
  CurrentTask: <task-id>
  CurrentPhase: <phase>
  LastStep: <last-successful-step>
  NextAction: <next-action>
  Status: <STATUS>
  Started: <ISO-8601>
  LastUpdated: <ISO-8601>

Recovery:
  On crash:
    Read current state
    Resume from exact state
    Do NOT restart workflow

Checkpoints (Phase 149, r3 round 3 — LangGraph thread_id model):
  Definition:
    A durable snapshot of chain-run state persisted BEFORE each arm
    transition, keyed by chain-run ID. Upgrades skip_if_complete flags
    to true resume-from-state.
  Schema:
    checkpoint_id: CPR-<run>-<seq>
    run_id: chain-run identifier (thread key)
    arm: current arm (P1/D1/S1/C1/R1/DEP1/RS1)
    step: execution trace step #01-#16
    state: typed shared-state snapshot (see shared-state.sdd schema)
    inputs: arm inputs (references, not inline blobs)
    outputs: arm outputs (compressed)
    iteration: per-arm iteration counter
    outcome: TypedOutcomeCodes value (if arm completed)
    ts: ISO-8601
  BoundaryDiscipline:
    rule: checkpoints at ARM BOUNDARIES and before INTERRUPTS only —
      never per-message (>75% of turns carry no recovery-relevant
      state; Crab study — blanket checkpointing is waste)
    rule: completed steps are NEVER re-executed on resume
  Storage: .specdd/checkpoints/{run_id}/ (runtime-only, git-ignored)
  Retention: last checkpoint per arm + final; intermediate pruned

CircuitBreakers (Phase 149, r3 round 3 — 3-layer failure stack):
  Layer1_retry:
    rule: transient failures retry with exponential backoff + jitter
    cap: 3 retries (~97.3% of transient failures caught; beyond 5 <0.5%)
  Layer2_fallback:
    rule: persistent failure switches provider/model/degraded path
  Layer3_breaker:
    definition: per-arm breaker opens above failure threshold within window
    config: threshold 3 failures / 10 min window per arm
    states: CLOSED -> OPEN (cooldown, default 15 min) -> HALF_OPEN (probe)
    rule: OPEN arm receives NO dispatches; hub routes to fallback or
      returns degraded fragment
    rule: breaker events are logged + traced (OTel span attributes)

Rules:
  [RT1] Agent state MUST be persisted after each step.
  [RT2] Crash recovery MUST resume from exact state.
  [RT3] Agent MUST NOT restart workflow on recovery.
  [RT4] Checkpoints MUST be created before risky operations.
  [RT5] Session MUST be persisted on every state change.
  [RT6] Session MUST be resumable after crash.
  [RT7] Session history MUST be retained for audit.
  [RT8] Checkpoints are written at arm boundaries and pre-interrupt —
         never per-message (boundary discipline).
  [RT9] Completed steps are never re-executed on checkpoint resume.
  [RT10] Per-arm circuit breakers precede chain-level iteration caps.
  [RT11] Breaker OPEN means no dispatch to that arm until cooldown ends.

State: +
